tim: 84 confirms over 30 days, 165.9 U committed
  windows containing a low 42, severe 12
  sensitivity median 111 mg/dL/U (41 to 216)
  multiplier uniform on [0.4, 1.0], 3000 replicates, 14 cores

==============================================================================
1. WHAT THE CONFIRM ITSELF CONTRIBUTES BY THE TIME OF THE NADIR
==============================================================================
  The recorded insulin on board is a NET figure and is negative on a quarter of
  cycles, so it cannot be the denominator of a share. Reported instead: the
  confirm's own bolus still present, and the glucose deficit the model attributes
  to it, against the fall actually observed.

  quantity                                         median          quartiles
  confirm's own bolus still on board at nadir (U)     0.15     0.00 to 0.58
  glucose deficit attributed to it by then (mg/dL)   163.04   103.18 to 229.03
  observed fall, peak to nadir (mg/dL)             123.50    84.75 to 153.25
  net insulin on board at the nadir (U)              0.35     0.09 to 0.79

  ratio of attributed deficit to observed fall: median 1.34
  A ratio near or above one means the model already accounts for the whole fall,
  and the confirm is the plausible cause. Well below one means other insulin,
  or the meal ending, did most of it and reducing the confirm will not prevent it.
    ratio 0.0-0.5:   9 confirms,   7 with a low
    ratio 0.5-1.0:  16 confirms,  10 with a low
    ratio 1.0-3.1:  59 confirms,  25 with a low

